    "created_at": "2016-05-06T20:37:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-06T20:38:05Z",
    "body": "> In particular, the spec should clarifies if fragment navigations, javascript: navigations and other types of navigations are allowed in the unload handlers\n\nThese are all navigations (i.e. they go through the navigate algorithm), so what about the current spec is unclear?\n\n> Also, if history manipulation via pushState is allowed or not. Different browsers behave differently with respect to that.\n\nThese are not navigations (they do not go through the navigate algorithm), so they are not blocked. How can we make this clearer?\n\nIt sounds like maybe what would help you is a non-normative note at the top of the navigate algorithm explaining in what cases it is called?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
