    "created_at": "2016-05-17T18:14:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-17T18:14:17Z",
    "body": "Sorry for the late reply.\n\nQuoting the spec: \"If there is a preexisting attempt to navigate browsingContext, and the source browsing context is the same as browsingContext, and that attempt is currently running the unload a document algorithm, and the origin of the URL of the resource being loaded in that navigation is not the same origin as the origin of the URL of resource, then abort these steps without affecting the preexisting attempt to navigate browsingContext.\"\n\nThe point that I think is not very clear is \"and the origin of the URL of the resource being loaded in that navigation is not the same origin as the origin of the URL of resource\", what happens when they are same origin? In particular, this would affect in-page navigations and javascript: navigations.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
