    "updated_at": "2016-05-17T21:29:33Z",
    "body": "Oh, I see! I am very sorry for not recognizing that was the important distinction here. You are right that it looks like currently same-origin navigations are allowed during the unload event (as long as it is not part of history traversal).\n\nIf Chromium is interested in disallowing _all_ navigations during the unload event, that would certainly simplify the spec, and be a very nice change. If you can prove web compatibility we're happy to make it.\n\nI believe that would collapse the current steps 2-4 into a single:\n\n> If there is a preexisting attempt to navigate browsingContext, and the source browsing context is the same as browsingContext, and that attempt is currently running the unload a document algorithm, then abort these steps without affecting the preexisting attempt to navigate browsingContext.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
